        "original_id": "0c144e6d-f539-5bbd-8f40-e33c30754631",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Lotus 49, Cosworth DFV\n- People: Colin Chapman, Maurice Philippe\n- Companies: Ford, Lotus Cars\n- Works: 9 Days in Summer\n- Topics: Formula One, automotive engineering\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony Colin Bruce Chapman CBE was born on 19 May 1928 and later became an influential English design engineer, inventor, and builder in the automotive industry.\n- Colin Chapman founded Lotus Cars.\n- The Lotus 49 was a Formula One racing car designed by Colin Chapman and Maurice Philippe for the 1967 Formula One season.\n- In 1967, the Lotus 49 took part in nine Formula One races.\n- Ford funded the development of the Cosworth DFV and the Lotus 49.\n- 9 Days in Summer is a promotional documentary film made by Ford about the development of the Ford-funded Cosworth DFV and Lotus 49, and its title refers to the nine Formula One races entered by the Lotus 49 in 1967.\n- Colin Chapman died on 16 December 1982.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cce03d7b-ad69-500e-b140-65202b6705be",
        "text": "Page: Lotus 49. Sentence: The Lotus 49 was a Formula One racing car designed by Colin Chapman and Maurice Philippe for the 1967 F1 season.\nPage: Colin Chapman. Sentence: Anthony Colin Bruce Chapman CBE (19 May 1928 – 16 December 1982) was an influential English design engineer, inventor, and builder in the automotive industry, and founder of Lotus Cars.\nPage: 9 Days in Summer. Sentence: 9 Days in Summer is a promotional documentary film made by Ford that tells the story of the development of the Ford-funded Cosworth DFV and Lotus 49, the title coming from the nine Formula One races the car took part in 1967, which are also extensively featured in the film.",
